# GSP355: Create and Manage Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL Instances - Challenge Lab (Foolproof Guide)

---

## Step 0: Setup Variables (Zero Typing Required)

Copy and paste this entire block directly into **Cloud Shell**. It pulls the region, zone, project ID, and username straight from Google Cloud metadata so nothing is typed by hand.

```bash
# Pull Zone and Region from project metadata
export ZONE=$(gcloud compute project-info describe --format="value(commonInstanceMetadata.items[google-compute-default-zone])")
export REGION=$(gcloud compute project-info describe --format="value(commonInstanceMetadata.items[google-compute-default-region])")

# Fallback: derive region from zone if needed
if [ -z "$REGION" ] && [ -n "$ZONE" ]; then
  export REGION=${ZONE%-*}
fi

# Set project context and student account
export PROJECT_ID=$(gcloud config get-value project)
export DB_USER=$(gcloud config get-value account)
export DB_NAME="orders"
export MIGRATION_JOB="orders-migration"
export CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE="postgres-orders"

# Set defaults to prevent empty parameter errors
gcloud config set compute/region "$REGION"
gcloud config set compute/zone "$ZONE"

# Print variables to verify
echo "----------------------------------------"
echo "PROJECT ID : $PROJECT_ID"
echo "ZONE       : $ZONE"
echo "REGION     : $REGION"
echo "USER       : $DB_USER"
echo "INSTANCE   : $CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE"
echo "----------------------------------------"
Task 1: Migrate Standalone PostgreSQL to Cloud SQL
1. Fix Database Tables on the Source VM
PostgreSQL replication will fail if any table lacks a primary key. Run this to SSH into the VM, fix the table, and exit:

Bash
gcloud compute ssh postgres-vm --zone=$ZONE
Inside postgres-vm, run:

Bash
sudo -u postgres psql -d orders -c "ALTER TABLE distribution_centers ADD PRIMARY KEY (id);"
sudo -u postgres psql -d orders -c "CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS pglogical;"
exit
2. Create Migration Profile & Start Job
Run this back in Cloud Shell:

Bash
# Get VM internal IP
VM_INTERNAL_IP=$(gcloud compute instances describe postgres-vm --zone=$ZONE --format='get(networkInterfaces[0].networkIP)')

# Create DMS connection profile
gcloud database-migration connection-profiles create postgresql postgres-vm-profile \
    --region=$REGION \
    --host=$VM_INTERNAL_IP \
    --port=5432 \
    --username=postgres \
    --password="supersecret!" \
    --provider=POSTGRESQL

# Create continuous migration job
gcloud database-migration migration-jobs create $MIGRATION_JOB \
    --region=$REGION \
    --source=postgres-vm-profile \
    --destination-instance-id=$CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE \
    --type=CONTINUOUS \
    --connectivity-vpc=default

# Start the migration job
gcloud database-migration migration-jobs start $MIGRATION_JOB --region=$REGION
