Task 2: Promote Cloud SQL to Stand-Alone Instance
1. Monitor the Sync Status
Before promoting, the migration job must finish its initial dump and enter the active change data capture (CDC) phase:

Bash
watch -n 5 "gcloud database-migration migration-jobs describe $MIGRATION_JOB --region=\$(gcloud config get-value compute/region) --format='table(state,phase)'"
Look at the table in your terminal:

Wait until STATE shows RUNNING and PHASE shows CDC (Change Data Capture).

Once you see this, press Ctrl + C on your keyboard to exit the loop.

2. Promote the Instance
Run this command in Cloud Shell:

Bash
gcloud database-migration migration-jobs promote $MIGRATION_JOB --region=$REGION --quiet
Wait about 90 to 120 seconds for the instance to detach. To check if it's done, run:

Bash
gcloud sql instances describe $CLOUD_SQL_INSTANCE --format="value(state)"
